WEBVTT

00:00.750 --> 00:03.230
Does everyone have their glasses?

00:03.520 --> 00:06.150
Professor, if you would please begin.

00:07.200 --> 00:10.000
First, as the rumors have suggested,

00:10.000 --> 00:12.150
the hospital's current 
director, Lord Shalbard,

00:12.150 --> 00:15.240
will be retiring at the end of next month.

00:15.240 --> 00:18.700
The election for the vacant 
position will be held soon.

00:19.490 --> 00:23.010
Our faction is the largest in the hospital.

00:23.010 --> 00:25.330
We have more than enough votes.

00:25.330 --> 00:28.450
In addition, one of the seven 
great aristocrats, Lord Fennel,

00:28.450 --> 00:31.420
has promised to spare no 
expense in his support.

00:32.790 --> 00:34.770
Bro, this is crazy!

00:34.770 --> 00:37.720
Things are getting totally crazy!

00:37.720 --> 00:39.720
I'm not your brother, though.

00:39.720 --> 00:42.410
Aw, don't be like that! Right, little sis?

00:42.410 --> 00:45.780
I wouldn't want a big 
brother like you, Cresson.

00:45.780 --> 00:47.120
Ice cold...

00:47.860 --> 00:52.230
I'm my brother's guest, but you 
don't have one, huh, Cresson?

00:53.010 --> 00:56.220
I just have too many potential 
girlfriends to narrow it down, is all.

00:56.220 --> 00:58.390
They all said no, huh?

00:58.390 --> 01:00.150
Poor Cresson.

01:00.150 --> 01:02.240
Don't just throw it in my face!

01:02.570 --> 01:04.800
Did you ask Umin?

01:04.800 --> 01:05.960
Huh?

01:05.960 --> 01:09.460
Why would I invite her of all people?

01:09.460 --> 01:12.890
Because you bug her all the time.

01:12.890 --> 01:17.720
And Carmilla told me that boys always 
bug the girls they like the most!

01:17.720 --> 01:19.680
Who the heck is Carmilla?

01:21.430 --> 01:24.750
It's fine! I've got my bro, Zeno.

01:24.750 --> 01:27.090
I'm gonna stick to him like glue!

01:27.090 --> 01:28.390
No, I'd rather you didn't.

01:30.820 --> 01:33.410
Those of you gathered here today

01:33.410 --> 01:36.290
are the chosen amongst 
all those in our group.

01:36.290 --> 01:37.570
Take pride in that!

01:38.240 --> 01:39.190
Cheers!

01:39.260 --> 01:41.450
Cheers!

01:41.450 --> 01:46.240
All right! Time to go suck up to the big shots!

01:47.310 --> 01:49.590
We'd better get to work, too.

01:49.590 --> 01:50.450
Yeah!

01:52.210 --> 01:55.920
<i>Afread went missing after being invited 
to a dinner party like this one.</i>

01:56.600 --> 01:59.260
<i>There was one thing I heard 
that caught my attention...</i>

02:00.260 --> 02:04.080
<i>At the time, Afread had been looking 
after Bons, who was drunk at that party.</i>

02:06.330 --> 02:08.350
You're Mr. Bons, right?

02:09.560 --> 02:11.140
Who the hell are you?

02:11.140 --> 02:13.570
I wanted to talk to you about something.

02:15.230 --> 02:18.990
At the last dinner party, there 
was a guy named Afread, right?

02:18.990 --> 02:22.990
Oh, the kid from the other research lab.

02:22.990 --> 02:27.030
I remember he brought me some 
water after I got hammered...

02:27.030 --> 02:28.960
Did you notice anything strange?

02:28.960 --> 02:30.990
Not that I remember!

02:30.990 --> 02:33.460
Next thing I knew, the sun was up.

02:33.840 --> 02:34.790
I see.

02:35.270 --> 02:38.220
He was a good kid, though.

02:38.220 --> 02:42.470
Most of these uppity types 
don't pay me any mind at all.

02:42.470 --> 02:48.850
Goldran tells 'em I'm a liar 
and to steer clear of me.

02:50.000 --> 02:53.610
<i>Why would he do that to the person he 
gave the position of first secretary to?</i>

02:53.610 --> 02:55.840
Not that I care.

02:55.840 --> 02:59.590
I owe the man my carefree 
lifestyle, after all.

02:59.590 --> 03:02.120
Let's hear it for our next hospital director!

03:03.120 --> 03:05.890
Why'd you become his secretary?

03:05.890 --> 03:07.680
We just go way back.

03:07.680 --> 03:08.860
How'd you meet?

03:08.860 --> 03:10.460
Well...

03:11.990 --> 03:14.690
What's it matter? Leave me alone.

03:15.790 --> 03:17.730
He's totally hammered.

03:17.730 --> 03:20.090
He doesn't seem to remember anything.

03:20.390 --> 03:23.850
But I think he does know something.

03:29.350 --> 03:32.340
Let's see if we can get him 
a little bit more drunk.

03:48.040 --> 03:55.550
<b>The Brilliant Healer's
New Life in the Shadows</b>

05:05.820 --> 05:07.650
Uh-huh, uh-huh. Go on.

05:07.650 --> 05:08.820
It's like I said!

05:08.820 --> 05:12.190
When I was younger, I wanted 
to be a photographer!

05:12.190 --> 05:13.290
Wow.

05:13.290 --> 05:15.960
I know, ain't I amazing?!

05:16.270 --> 05:18.480
You really are.

05:18.480 --> 05:22.590
Y'know, back when I was younger...

05:19.760 --> 05:22.590
Lily, what is this?

05:22.590 --> 05:26.560
If a man is drinking, and a girl 
tells him how impressive he is,

05:26.560 --> 05:29.850
he'll get full of himself 
and just keep talking!

05:29.850 --> 05:32.250
And who taught you this?

05:32.250 --> 05:33.550
Carmilla.

05:33.550 --> 05:35.410
That stupid specter...

05:35.850 --> 05:40.190
Say, Mr. Bons, what happened that 
time Afread brought you water?

05:41.150 --> 05:45.440
If I remember right, we went 
outside to get some fresh air.

05:45.440 --> 05:48.880
Great idea. Let's see if 
that'll sober you up some.

05:53.020 --> 05:55.330
What're you gonna do, Zenos?

05:55.670 --> 05:57.100
I had an idea.

05:57.630 --> 06:01.120
What if we re-create the same 
situation as with Afread?

06:10.370 --> 06:14.970
Hey, Goldran, look! 
Just like back in the day.

06:14.970 --> 06:17.650
<i>Does he think I'm Goldran?</i>

06:18.140 --> 06:23.220
You're gonna be nobility once you're 
director of the Royal Hospital, right?

06:23.850 --> 06:27.360
Looks like you've got an in 
with Lord Fennel again, huh?

06:27.360 --> 06:28.990
<i>"Again"?</i>

06:28.990 --> 06:31.970
Come on, don't play dumb!

06:31.970 --> 06:37.370
That day thirteen years ago is 
why you are who you are now!

06:37.370 --> 06:39.500
What day thirteen years ago?

06:39.500 --> 06:41.750
Come on, don't tell me you forgot!

06:41.750 --> 06:44.470
Uh... no, I haven't.

06:44.470 --> 06:47.380
Man, it's been thirteen years already, huh?

06:47.380 --> 06:53.570
The day your life changed, after getting 
nowhere with your research for so long!

06:53.570 --> 06:56.670
The day of the explosion!

06:56.670 --> 06:57.640
Right...

06:58.020 --> 07:02.920
Lord Fennel's backing got you a spot 
as a professor at the Royal Hospital!

07:02.920 --> 07:05.420
And this time, you're gonna be director!

07:05.420 --> 07:08.460
You are a slick one!

07:14.540 --> 07:16.650
What now, Zenos?

07:16.650 --> 07:20.140
I feel like we're on the verge 
of something important,

07:20.140 --> 07:22.070
but he's not waking up, 
so I guess we're done.

07:22.880 --> 07:26.460
We'll leave him with one of 
the staff and take a break.

07:30.320 --> 07:32.570
Are you done gathering info?

07:34.350 --> 07:36.560
I feel like I missed something...

07:36.560 --> 07:38.140
I see!

07:38.140 --> 07:40.000
You scared me...

07:38.810 --> 07:42.140
Allow me to reveal this mystery to you.

07:42.140 --> 07:43.800
What are you doing here?

07:43.800 --> 07:45.630
This mansion is crawling with healers.

07:45.630 --> 07:46.980
Being a nuisance.

07:46.980 --> 07:50.520
And being a nuisance is the most 
entertaining when it's the most dangerous!

07:50.520 --> 07:53.580
That doesn't even make sense. 
Why look so smug about it?

07:53.580 --> 07:56.130
Can you figure out what happened, Carmilla?

07:56.130 --> 07:57.370
Indeed.

07:57.370 --> 08:01.310
That drunk's rambling gave me 
the gist of what's going on.

08:01.310 --> 08:05.760
I'll have you know, despite appearances, 
I was a world-famous sage.

08:05.760 --> 08:10.240
No mystery remains concealed 
from my unparalleled intellect!

08:10.240 --> 08:11.880
Wow, really?

08:11.880 --> 08:12.960
Not at all.

08:12.960 --> 08:14.760
Why would you lie about that?

08:19.010 --> 08:22.120
Is Doc gonna be back anytime soon?

08:22.120 --> 08:24.040
Lynga thinks he will.

08:24.040 --> 08:27.730
I feel like I'm going to 
turn to stone from waiting.

08:27.730 --> 08:31.410
What are you two even doing here every day?

08:31.410 --> 08:35.240
Don't you have people to look 
after instead of loafing around?

08:35.240 --> 08:37.300
Lynga knows you're only saying that

08:37.300 --> 08:42.370
so you can sniff Sir Zenos's pillow in 
secret once you're the only one here.

08:42.370 --> 08:46.210
What?! You've been doing 
that, Zophia?! I'm jealous!

08:46.210 --> 08:48.750
I am not like the two of you!

08:48.750 --> 08:51.180
All right, enough of that.

08:51.180 --> 08:54.630
No point in facing off with you 
two when he's not even here.

08:54.630 --> 08:55.920
Agreed.

08:55.920 --> 08:59.080
He'd be upset with us if we got 
injured in the process, anyway.

09:01.520 --> 09:04.770
Boss! Zonde got hurt real bad in an accident!

09:04.770 --> 09:05.840
What happened?

09:05.840 --> 09:08.860
While we were working, a pillar 
broke, and it went through his gut!

09:08.860 --> 09:11.360
When will Doc be back?

09:11.360 --> 09:14.830
Lynga thinks if we wait for 
Sir Zenos, it'll be too late.

09:14.830 --> 09:18.620
I agree. We need to take him 
to Zenos as soon as we can.

09:18.620 --> 09:20.680
We can't.

09:20.680 --> 09:23.560
The doc's undercover with a fake identity.

09:23.560 --> 09:25.250
We'd ruin the whole thing.

09:25.250 --> 09:27.420
Lynga understands how you feel,

09:27.420 --> 09:29.280
but this is an emergency.

09:29.280 --> 09:31.630
Can you picture Zenos getting upset about it?

09:35.010 --> 09:36.880
Let's get ready to go!

09:36.880 --> 09:39.530
And we're going to pay him 
double his usual rate!

09:40.730 --> 09:43.680
The day of an explosion, thirteen years ago...

09:43.680 --> 09:47.020
It was the day a man, who had been an 
unremarkable researcher before then,

09:47.020 --> 09:50.110
found his life had changed 
after saving a noble's life.

09:50.560 --> 09:53.570
When you hear of someone owing 
a healer, what do you picture?

09:53.570 --> 09:57.760
The normal thing is to assume 
the healer healed them.

09:57.760 --> 10:01.580
So some kind of explosion happened 
where Lord Fennel got hurt...

10:01.580 --> 10:04.110
And Goldran healed him, I assume?

10:04.110 --> 10:06.730
If it were that simple, it'd be a sweet story.

10:06.730 --> 10:10.330
But consider how this story is kept secret.

10:10.330 --> 10:12.320
Why isn't it better known?

10:12.320 --> 10:14.280
Circumstances best kept secret, I'd wager.

10:14.280 --> 10:15.920
What circumstances?

10:15.920 --> 10:17.840
If there was an explosion,

10:17.840 --> 10:20.590
we can assume the noble 
had been hurt fairly badly.

10:20.590 --> 10:25.390
Yet, Zenos, the person you met 
seemed to be right as rain.

10:25.390 --> 10:29.060
Is that kind of complete healing possible?

10:29.060 --> 10:32.150
I mean, as long as the heart's intact, 
you could probably manage.

10:32.150 --> 10:34.610
I wasn't asking about 
your extraordinary case.

10:34.610 --> 10:37.290
Could this Goldran have managed it?

10:39.070 --> 10:40.720
I think I get it!

10:41.450 --> 10:44.460
Thirteen years ago, there was an explosion,

10:44.460 --> 10:46.950
and the aristocrat got hurt...

10:46.950 --> 10:50.330
But the person who healed him 
didn't take credit for it,

10:50.330 --> 10:55.390
and when that person wandered off, 
Mr. Goldran happened to show up.

10:55.390 --> 10:58.550
He made it seem to the aristocrat that 
he was the one who did the healing.

10:58.550 --> 11:00.940
Mr. Bons saw it all happen

11:00.940 --> 11:03.680
and used it to blackmail Mr. Goldran!

11:03.680 --> 11:07.260
But how does that tie into 
Afread's disappearance?

11:08.600 --> 11:13.690
Maybe Mr. Bons got drunk at that 
dinner party, like this time,

11:13.690 --> 11:16.690
and he told Afread the truth.

11:16.970 --> 11:22.350
Then he went into hiding because 
he was scared that Mr. Bons

11:22.350 --> 11:25.330
would remember he told him... maybe?

11:26.430 --> 11:28.950
Very impressive, Lily!

11:28.950 --> 11:31.680
Maybe I could be a detective!

11:31.680 --> 11:35.200
Zenos's clinic and Lily's detective agency!

11:35.200 --> 11:37.470
The mystery is unraveled!

11:38.950 --> 11:40.800
There you guys are!

11:40.800 --> 11:43.000
Since I got a few ins with the bigwigs,

11:43.000 --> 11:45.430
I figured I'd introduce you two to them!

11:45.430 --> 11:48.570
I don't want a big brother 
who's a brown-noser.

11:48.570 --> 11:51.760
I will demonstrate how to be a success 
in the world to you, little sis.

11:51.760 --> 11:53.060
Come along!

11:55.770 --> 11:58.660
What are you going to do, Zenos?

11:58.660 --> 11:59.900
About what?

11:59.900 --> 12:01.510
You know what I mean.

12:01.510 --> 12:04.160
You mean the other possibility...

12:04.160 --> 12:06.410
Then you did notice it.

12:06.410 --> 12:08.880
Hearing you describe it made me catch on.

12:08.880 --> 12:10.760
From the sound of this explosion,

12:10.760 --> 12:13.660
I doubted that Lord Fennel 
would be the only victim.

12:14.160 --> 12:18.020
A crowd of injured people, one of them 
looking more put-together than the rest.

12:18.020 --> 12:21.730
Goldran sought out a noble in 
order to get them in his debt.

12:21.730 --> 12:25.010
That's where his life 
transfer magic comes in.

12:25.460 --> 12:29.760
If he transferred the remaining life 
force from all those injured...

12:29.760 --> 12:31.890
Goldran would've chosen who survived.

12:31.890 --> 12:34.020
And that's a crime?

12:34.020 --> 12:36.990
Triage wouldn't be a crime.

12:36.990 --> 12:41.030
But to sacrifice other people to save one...

12:41.030 --> 12:42.090
That's just...

12:43.280 --> 12:46.280
But if anyone survived what happened,

12:46.680 --> 12:50.230
and it was Afread... he probably 
wouldn't accept what Goldran did.

12:50.230 --> 12:51.980
Vengeance, then?

12:51.980 --> 12:53.910
It's a possibility.

12:54.540 --> 12:57.430
Afread... Where in the world are you?

12:58.630 --> 13:01.160
So, what will you do?

13:01.160 --> 13:03.760
Just tell Becker what I've learned.

13:03.760 --> 13:05.880
Judgment isn't my job.

13:05.880 --> 13:07.800
I'm just an underground healer.

13:07.800 --> 13:09.720
I suppose that's true.

13:11.030 --> 13:12.730
Thanks, Carmilla.

13:12.730 --> 13:13.820
Huh?

13:13.820 --> 13:16.480
You came to check up on me 
because you were worried, right?

13:16.480 --> 13:18.610
And thanks to you, I've figured some stuff out.

13:18.610 --> 13:22.480
Fool! I only came to be a 
nuisance, to entertain myself.

13:22.480 --> 13:25.500
Consider my debt to you for 
the zombie king matter repaid.

13:29.440 --> 13:30.300
What the...

13:31.280 --> 13:32.490
What's up?

13:32.490 --> 13:36.050
Bro. There seems to be some 
kinda commotion outside.

13:39.120 --> 13:41.590
Wait, isn't that Umin?

13:43.570 --> 13:44.590
I'm trying to tell you...

13:44.590 --> 13:47.040
I just need to speak with someone named Zeno!

13:47.040 --> 13:49.330
No one enters without an invitation!

13:49.330 --> 13:52.600
Then could you please call him over? 
It's a bit of an emergency.

13:52.600 --> 13:54.330
The professor is hosting this party!

13:54.330 --> 13:55.660
You don't get to interrupt it.

13:55.660 --> 13:56.750
Excuse me!

13:58.710 --> 13:59.850
Loewe?!

14:00.360 --> 14:02.730
What is she doing here?

14:02.730 --> 14:06.770
Idiot! Why would you holler like 
that where everyone can hear?!

14:06.770 --> 14:08.490
What other choice is there?

14:08.490 --> 14:12.740
Plenty! We can't get the doc in trouble.

14:12.740 --> 14:15.710
No, Lynga thinks Loewe is right.

14:15.710 --> 14:18.750
We don't have enough time 
to take things slow.

14:18.750 --> 14:21.330
The others are here, too.

14:21.330 --> 14:22.680
Yeah...

14:23.500 --> 14:25.540
Are those demihumans?

14:25.540 --> 14:29.090
What are those lesser creatures 
doing at my mansion?

14:29.090 --> 14:30.970
Throw them out at once!

14:39.980 --> 14:42.110
There you are, Zenos.

14:42.110 --> 14:44.250
Sorry, but it's an emergency!

14:44.250 --> 14:47.990
Zeno...s? Wait, the special research student?

14:47.990 --> 14:50.880
Does he know these demihumans?

14:50.880 --> 14:52.240
What happened?

14:52.240 --> 14:54.280
Zonde is hurt badly.

14:54.280 --> 14:56.250
We were headed to the Royal Hospital dorms,

14:56.250 --> 15:00.120
but we ran into the glasses girl, 
and she told us where you were.

15:00.120 --> 15:02.880
Uh... Yes, that's right.

15:02.880 --> 15:06.500
Hey! What exactly is your relationship 
with these demihumans?

15:06.500 --> 15:09.090
B-Bro... Say it ain't so...

15:09.090 --> 15:11.340
Loewe, what's Zonde's condition?

15:11.340 --> 15:13.080
His breathing is pretty shallow.

15:13.080 --> 15:14.850
Doc!

15:14.850 --> 15:17.020
I'm sorry! I'm so sorry!

15:18.620 --> 15:21.530
I didn't wanna mess with your plans...

15:21.530 --> 15:25.480
But Zonde... It looks like he's gonna die...

15:25.480 --> 15:28.410
I'm begging you... Save him.

15:29.490 --> 15:31.490
All right. I'm on my way.

15:31.490 --> 15:34.080
Hold it! Are you insane?!

15:34.080 --> 15:36.550
No, I'm definitely sane.

15:36.550 --> 15:40.240
Impossible! After securing your 
path to glory among my faction,

15:40.240 --> 15:43.120
you'd lower yourself to save 
these demihuman peasants?!

15:43.120 --> 15:44.880
If you go, there's no coming back!

15:44.880 --> 15:46.460
Suit yourself.

15:46.460 --> 15:52.340
You don't realize what you're throwing 
away! A path to becoming elite!

15:52.870 --> 15:55.850
I'm not interested in being 
part of an elite faction.

15:56.360 --> 15:58.600
I'm just a healer.

15:58.960 --> 16:00.460
That's all I've ever been.

16:01.350 --> 16:04.030
Look after yourself, Cresson.

16:05.140 --> 16:06.550
Lily, come on.

16:06.550 --> 16:08.080
Okay. Up I go!

16:15.240 --> 16:17.740
Bro... How could you?

16:18.260 --> 16:22.120
You're not as big a fool as he is, I take it?

16:22.480 --> 16:24.470
His future is done for.

16:24.470 --> 16:27.730
I'll make sure he never 
works as a healer again.

16:28.610 --> 16:31.670
You're right. He's a fool.

16:31.670 --> 16:35.710
I want to get promoted... get a 
nice house... have a hot woman...

16:35.710 --> 16:38.220
That's what I've been working for all along.

16:40.640 --> 16:44.600
But whether it was a dog or the 
daughter of a major aristocrat, he...

16:46.630 --> 16:51.150
No one likes me anyway, and I'm 
greedy, and people think I'm stupid,

16:51.150 --> 16:52.090
but even so...

16:53.610 --> 16:56.820
I'm a healer, too, damn it!

16:56.820 --> 16:58.060
What?!

17:01.000 --> 17:06.380
I, Cresson Wembley, have to withdraw 
from the faction due to circumstances!

17:08.290 --> 17:13.420
Bro! Wait up! I'll help with the healing!

17:16.300 --> 17:18.780
I'm so... sorry...

17:18.780 --> 17:19.910
It's fine.

17:20.430 --> 17:22.950
I'm sorry about this, Doc.

17:22.950 --> 17:26.690
It's okay. I'm sorry I was missing for so long.

17:26.690 --> 17:30.650
See? Just like I said, Sir Zenos doesn't mind.

17:30.650 --> 17:31.690
Indeed.

17:32.820 --> 17:34.090
We're almost done.

17:34.690 --> 17:37.820
Here's Cresson! Let me help with the...

17:39.320 --> 17:43.250
Aw, come on! Why'd I even quit?!

17:43.250 --> 17:45.380
You're as stupid as ever.

17:45.380 --> 17:47.080
Sh-Shut up!

17:47.360 --> 17:49.870
But I heard what you said.

17:49.870 --> 17:54.260
You may be stupid, but that was also the 
most impressed I've ever been with you.

17:54.260 --> 17:58.640
Sh-Shut up! It's thanks to 
you guys I'm in this situation!

17:58.640 --> 18:00.490
So you'd better take responsibility.

18:00.490 --> 18:02.930
Maybe you really are just unpleasant.

18:04.230 --> 18:07.270
That's right! I'm as bad as they come!

18:07.270 --> 18:10.100
Who's the kid, Doc?

18:11.450 --> 18:13.270
How do I put this?

18:15.460 --> 18:18.750
He's like a pesky little brother, I guess.

18:23.150 --> 18:24.790
I see.

18:25.050 --> 18:30.190
Afread had mentioned being caught 
in a major accident as a child.

18:30.190 --> 18:32.750
This may have been what he was referring to.

18:32.750 --> 18:34.580
I had no idea...

18:35.420 --> 18:40.510
When is the party to celebrate Professor 
Goldran's election to the director's office?

18:40.510 --> 18:41.580
Tomorrow.

18:42.020 --> 18:45.970
Afread may take some action to get revenge.

18:46.820 --> 18:49.280
I should attend that party.

18:49.950 --> 18:52.400
Now, putting that aside...

18:52.400 --> 18:55.100
I appreciate you bringing me 
this valuable information.

18:55.100 --> 18:57.710
You've done your job, Zenos.

18:57.710 --> 18:59.160
Thank you for that.

18:59.680 --> 19:00.800
You sure?

19:00.800 --> 19:02.910
That was our arrangement, after all.

19:02.910 --> 19:05.870
You'll need to stay another 
day for the paperwork

19:05.870 --> 19:09.190
allowing your special research 
student period to end,

19:09.190 --> 19:13.690
so I'll provide your other payment—
regarding your teacher—tomorrow.

19:14.210 --> 19:16.130
All right. I understand.

19:16.750 --> 19:19.920
I'll come by your room this evening, then.

19:19.920 --> 19:22.260
Was there something else we needed to do?

19:22.260 --> 19:25.420
Why, your going-away party, of course!

19:31.380 --> 19:35.610
So Bro was hired by Professor Becker 
to investigate a disappearance,

19:35.610 --> 19:37.780
and normally runs a clinic in 
an abandoned part of the city,

19:37.780 --> 19:41.280
which is how he knows demihumans? For real?

19:41.280 --> 19:43.160
Yep. All true.

19:43.160 --> 19:47.640
What am I supposed to do when you're gone?!

19:47.640 --> 19:49.380
This is just pitiful.

19:49.380 --> 19:50.930
That's harsh, classmate!

19:50.930 --> 19:53.040
Don't you agree, little sis?

19:53.040 --> 19:55.380
I don't want a pitiful big brother.

19:55.380 --> 19:57.380
Even my little sister is harsh!

19:57.380 --> 19:59.380
Come on, Bro!

19:59.380 --> 20:03.130
You're adaptable enough to 
survive wherever you end up.

20:03.130 --> 20:07.640
That doesn't feel like a full compliment... 
What do you think, little sis?

20:07.640 --> 20:10.000
Lily isn't actually my little sister.

20:10.000 --> 20:11.640
Seriously?!

20:11.640 --> 20:13.760
I'm sorry for lying, Cresson.

20:13.760 --> 20:16.950
I'm actually Zenos's wife!

20:16.950 --> 20:18.800
F-For real?!

20:18.800 --> 20:20.530
No, not for real.

20:20.530 --> 20:21.950
I must be losing it...

20:21.950 --> 20:25.530
I'm even seeing something that looks 
like a wraith behind that pillar.

20:27.280 --> 20:29.280
Why did you come out, Carmilla?

20:29.280 --> 20:31.290
How could I not?

20:31.290 --> 20:34.420
That boy is drowning in my liquor!

20:34.420 --> 20:36.750
It's just some stuff you 
snuck out of Goldran's house.

20:36.750 --> 20:39.960
That wine desires to be drunk by me.

20:39.960 --> 20:41.020
Zenos?

20:42.090 --> 20:43.850
Don't worry, it's fine.

20:43.850 --> 20:45.130
She's got a good heart.

20:45.390 --> 20:48.530
A good-hearted... wraith? What?

20:49.420 --> 20:52.780
You're the only one I'd allow to 
speak about me in such a way.

20:53.640 --> 20:55.220
Do not drink all of it.

20:55.220 --> 20:57.900
If you do, I'll curse you and your descendants.

21:08.320 --> 21:10.540
What has you spacing out?

21:11.000 --> 21:14.920
I'm from the slums, and was treated 
terribly by the party I worked with,

21:14.920 --> 21:17.380
but the two of them don't 
treat me any different.

21:17.380 --> 21:20.430
Finding out people like that 
exist is a bit of a relief.

21:20.880 --> 21:22.880
Sad to part with them?

21:23.380 --> 21:27.260
Could be. But I'm used to saying goodbye.

21:27.780 --> 21:31.800
Meeting people, parting with them, 
and meeting again, should it be fated.

21:32.320 --> 21:35.360
That cycle, repeated, is human life itself.

21:35.360 --> 21:38.770
It's how we learn the width 
and depth of the world.

21:39.060 --> 21:42.280
You actually make sense occasionally.

21:42.280 --> 21:44.860
You learn a thing or two
after living for 300 years.

21:44.860 --> 21:46.460
Except you're dead.

21:49.940 --> 21:52.240
Well, I appreciate everything.

21:52.240 --> 21:55.680
You're the one who's helped us.

21:55.680 --> 21:57.010
Bro!

21:57.010 --> 21:58.000
Oh, right!

21:58.000 --> 22:03.460
Dr. Becker asked me to give you a letter 
containing the details about your teacher.

22:07.930 --> 22:10.740
This... was inside his desk...

22:12.640 --> 22:14.220
What the...

23:55.580 --> 24:00.040
Choosing Who Lives

23:57.240 --> 23:58.720
"Choosing Who Lives."
